# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Installed Dependencies
- Added `@vercel/analytics` package (version 2.0.1) via npm
- Updated `package.json` to include the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Modified Files

**web/app/layout.js**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next';`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag in the RootLayout component
- This follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router setup

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide for Next.js App Router projects:
- Fetched latest documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart
- Identified this as a Next.js App Router project (uses app/layout.js)
- Used npm as the package manager (package-lock.json present)
- Added the Analytics component to the root layout as recommended

## Testing

- Successfully built the project with `npm run build`
- Build completed without errors or warnings
- All routes compiled successfully (7 static pages)
- No TypeScript or ESLint errors introduced

## Next Steps

To activate analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy this project to Vercel
2. Navigate to the Analytics tab in your Vercel dashboard
3. Select your project and click "Enable" to activate Web Analytics
4. Analytics will start collecting data after deployment

The Analytics component is now ready and will automatically start tracking page views once enabled in the Vercel dashboard.
